==================== Input ====================
// Duplicate keys keep their relative order, so JSON's last-one-wins semantics survive reordering.
//
// The sort is stable and equal keys tie, so `"first"` stays before `"last"` however the object moves.
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "paths": {
    "/p": { "get": { "responses": {}, "summary": "first", "operationId": "op", "summary": "last" } }
  }
}

==================== Output ====================
------------------
{ printWidth: 80 }
------------------
// Duplicate keys keep their relative order, so JSON's last-one-wins semantics survive reordering.
//
// The sort is stable and equal keys tie, so `"first"` stays before `"last"` however the object moves.
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "paths": {
    "/p": {
      "get": {
        "operationId": "op",
        "summary": "first",
        "summary": "last",
        "responses": {}
      }
    }
  }
}

-------------------
{ printWidth: 100 }
-------------------
// Duplicate keys keep their relative order, so JSON's last-one-wins semantics survive reordering.
//
// The sort is stable and equal keys tie, so `"first"` stays before `"last"` however the object moves.
{
  "openapi": "3.0.0",
  "paths": {
    "/p": { "get": { "operationId": "op", "summary": "first", "summary": "last", "responses": {} } }
  }
}

